## 📑 SECTION 9: SPEC-DRIVEN DEVELOPMENT PROTOCOL (NO CODE WITHOUT DOCS)

Before writing or modifying ANY code for a new Phase, Feature, Bugfix, or Architectural Change:
1. **Dedicated Docs Directory**: Create `docs/features/<feature-name>/` or `docs/tasks/<task-name>/`.
2. **`spec.md`**: Feature Overview, Current vs Proposed State, Architectural Trade-offs, Data Models & Contracts, Security & Edge Cases.
3. **`plan.md`**: Prerequisites, Granular Atomic Checklist (`[ ]`), Verification & Acceptance Criteria.
4. **Autonomous Atomic Task Execution**: When assigned or instructed to perform a task, execute the entire task end-to-end without asking for permission midway. NEVER seek user permission to create or update any files (author Spec & Plan -> Types/DTOs -> Entities/Repositories -> Domain Logic -> Controller -> Tests & Verification).
5. **Task Completion Gate**: Once the atomic task is verified and complete, tick off `[x]` in `ROADMAP.md`, report completion, test results, and suggested commit message, and STOP to wait for the user to tell the agent to move on to the next task.

